For $f: X subset.eq CC -> CC$ with $X subset.eq CC$, limits along the function and along sequences decide each other:

$
  f(z) -> y "as" z -> a quad & <=> quad f(z_n) -> y "for every" (z_n) "on" X \
  f(z) "diverges as" z -> a quad & <=> quad f(z_n) "diverges for every" (z_n) "on" X
$

where $(z_n) -> a$, each $z_n$ lies in $X$, and $(z_n)$ is not the constant sequence.
